# Configuration file for haveged
#
# This file configures the haveged package, which provides entropy via hardware-based
# random number generation using the HAVEged algorithm (HARDWARE entropy VEntor).
# It is typically used on headless servers (like VMs or embedded devices) that lack
# sufficient hardware entropy sources (/dev/random) for cryptographic operations.

# Options to pass to haveged:
# These arguments are appended to the haveged daemon startup command.
# Common options:
#   -w <int>   : Set the target fill-level for the entropy pool (default: 2048 bits).
#                Values below 2048 may cause issues with applications needing high entropy.
#   --watchdog : Enable hardware watchdog timer support.
#   -d         : Enable debug logging to stderr (useful for troubleshooting).
#   -c         : Print configuration and exit.
#
# See `man haveged` for a full list of available options.
# The default is usually sufficient for most use cases.
#DAEMON_ARGS="{{ args | default('close') }}"